# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) to override locally.

# Which analytics adapter to load. See src/lib/analytics/providers.js.
#   debug — logs to the console and window.__analytics; no network, no account.
#   none  — disables collection entirely.
# Defaults to `debug` in dev and `none` in production builds, so no data leaves
# the browser unless this is set deliberately.
VITE_ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=debug

# Note: browser DNT / Global Privacy Control signals are honoured and win over
# the setting above. If your own browser sends GPC you will see nothing locally;
# run `localStorage.setItem("analytics:force","1")` in the console to opt in.
# That override is compiled out of production builds.

# ── Error monitoring (src/lib/monitoring.js) ─────────────────────────────────
# Sentry DSN. Leave unset and Sentry is never loaded — its chunk is not even
# fetched. Unlike analytics above, this is NOT suppressed by DNT/GPC: crash
# reports are operational, not behavioural (sendDefaultPii is off, so no IP or
# cookies). An explicit `analytics:opt-out` in localStorage does disable it.
#
# ⚠ Setting this alone is not enough. The site ships `connect-src 'self'`, so
# reports are blocked until the Sentry ingest origin is added to the CSP in all
# four places — see the header comment in src/lib/monitoring.js.
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://<key>@<org>.ingest.us.sentry.io/<project>

# Commit SHA stamped onto Sentry events, so an error points at a release.
# VITE_RELEASE=
